  "status": "Application Received",
  "description": "We live within an old block of flats which have never had their windows replaced. We are proposing changing the current single glazing windows which were built and installed in the 60's to double glazing UPVC. We have chosen a like for like style, matching the current windows, as well as chosen a silver finish which matches the current aluminium exterior. All windows are restricted from view from any front façade. As part of this proposal we have also included plans to change one full length window to a door, again matching aesthetics. The door faces the rear of the property, similar to other doors that have been installed in the block. The door is to enable access at ground level, both myself and my partner have disabled parents so are unable to access the flat due to these being on the first floor. All approvals have been given in the form of an LTA from the housing association Freehold Guiness Trust ",
